# [[.Name]]

A GoVibe application: a Go module that depends on the framework (`[[.FrameworkModule]]`) and holds only application
code. It starts as the Hello GoVibe demo, ordinary app code in the usual layers that you keep as a smoke test or delete
when you build your own (`SKILL.md` says what to delete).

- `GET /` renders the landing page, with a button that uses htmx to call `/hello`.
- `GET /api/hello` returns `{"message":"Hello GoVibe!"}`.
- `GET /hello` returns the same greeting as plain text.

## Run
- `make dev`: the app with the dev tools compiled in. The page is at http://localhost:8080 and the dev panel at
  http://localhost:8080/dev (the project graph, the docs, the database explorer, the scheduler and the MCP server for agents).
- `make air`: the same, rebuilt on every change.
- `make test` and `make check`: what CI runs (`.github/workflows/govibe.yml`).
- `make build`: one binary with no dev tooling, `./[[.Name]]`; `./[[.Name]] help` lists its commands.

The rules of the code and the layout are in `SKILL.md`, the architecture in `docs/public/ARCHITECTURE.md` and the data in
`docs/public/MEMORY_SCHEMA.md`.
